X11: ignore a slave pointer's button events until the window also has keyboard focus.

With XInput2, SDL selects button events from every device. Under a click-to-focus window manager
(metacity, Mutter, Muffin), the window manager's passive grab takes the master pointer's press, but
the physical (slave) device's press still reaches SDL before the window has focus. The window
manager then focuses the window and replays the press through the master pointer. SDL's check for
slave events looks at mouse focus, which the pointer already gives the window, so both presses get
through: with SDL_HINT_MOUSE_FOCUS_CLICKTHROUGH set, a single click on an unfocused window arrives
as two clicks, the second counted as a double click. Without the hint, the replayed press is
dropped as the focusing click and the early slave press gets through instead, so the hint's
default doesn't hold under XInput2.

Checking keyboard focus too drops the early slave press. The replayed master press follows the
hint, as it does without XInput2.

--- a/src/video/x11/SDL_x11xinput2.c
+++ b/src/video/x11/SDL_x11xinput2.c
@@ -684,7 +684,7 @@
                 /* Ignore slave button events on non-focused windows, as they can arrive before FocusIn events,
                  * or result in focus being incorrectly set while a grab is active.
                  */
-                if (SDL_GetMouseFocus() != windowdata->window) {
+                if (SDL_GetMouseFocus() != windowdata->window || SDL_GetKeyboardFocus() != windowdata->window) {
                     break;
                 }
 
